                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Okay, okay, so it's not Portal.  I mean, it doesn't have portals for a start.  However, you do have a magnetic gun that can push and pull boxes, as well as pushing and pulling you.  So yes, it isn't Portal.  BUT Portal was a beautifully crafted game.  Had Portal not existed, I think people would be be much kinder towards this game.\r\n\r\nI found this a pretty good game and enjoyed the challenge.  I didn't much like the dystopian prison setting, and I agree with others, the voices over the tannoy isn't anywhere near as clever or funny as Portal.  (And sadly there wasn't a song at the end like Portal's lovely \"Still Alive\" song.)  \r\n\r\nThe difficulty level was just about right.  Some levels were pretty straight-forward but others were challenging, but not to the point where I needed a walkthrough or guide.  Once completed I didn't replay to try the different choices that were offered, but I'd be open to trying it again at another time.\r\n\r\nSo... should you get it?  Yes.  It's a decent game, and not expensive.  If it's on sale, even better.  And there's free DLC which I'm gonna give a go too.",
